Thread-local reads off the TCG hot paths (M9 track,
docs/tracks/m9-tcg-aarch64.md). On macOS every __thread access is a call into
dyld's TLS thunk (_tlv_get_addr), and a translation-bound guest (Moto Racer
1997's self-patching rasterizer, after patch 18) spent 8.8 % of its vCPU
thread there: 63 % of it the five nested rcu_read_lock()/unlock() pairs the
store slow path took per store into a page holding code (the dirty-bitmap
helpers each take the lock; the vCPU already holds it for the whole of
cpu_exec), the rest the translator reading tcg_ctx once per operand in the
optimizer (temp_idx) and two to three times per emitted op / temp / constant.
Now: notdirty_write uses _rcu_locked variants of the dirty-bitmap helpers
(cpu_exec_step_atomic gets the RCU read section it did not have, so every
caller holds one), and the tcg.c allocators read tcg_ctx once and pass it
down. No behaviour change; the DOS batteries and the XP guest stage are the
regression guard.

